Check step 2 for m,n finite: yes.

Need maybe include the exact T_{m,n} symbol. Use T_{m,n}. Then in final: 
T_{m,n}+T_{n,m}
= \frac{m^2n}{3^m(n3^m+m3^n)}+\frac{n^2m}{3^n(n3^m+m3^n)}
= \frac{mn(\frac{m}{3^m}+\frac{n}{3^n})}{n3^m+m3^n}
= \frac{\frac{m}{3^m}+\frac{n}{3^n}}{\frac{3^m}{m}+\frac{3^n}{n}}
= \frac{m}{3^m}\frac{n}{3^n}.
Need verify second equality: common denominator C = n3^m+m3^n. Yes. Then factor mn: C = mn(3^m/m+3^n/n). So ratio becomes (m/3^m+n/3^n)/(3^m/m+3^n/n). Then = product. Could show using reciprocals.
